IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpfta-types`
IMPORT `cpfta-part4-general`

-- Tests for Part 4 (ss 35 to 44).

§ `Tests -- Part 4`

§§ `35. No contracting out`

-- Contracting Out Facts: term in a contract or agreement to the contrary, inconsistent with the Act,
-- a waiver or release of a right under the Act, released in settlement of a dispute.
#ASSERT `the contract term is void to the extent that it is inconsistent with the Act` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the contract term is void to the extent that it is inconsistent with the Act` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the contract term is void to the extent that it is inconsistent with the Act` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the contract term is void to the extent that it is inconsistent with the Act` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `the waiver or release is void` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the waiver or release is void` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the waiver or release is void` (`Contracting Out Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `36. Rights transferred`

--                                                                              heir or assignee, receives goods or services, in the course of business
#ASSERT `the individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier` (`Successor Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier` (`Successor Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier` (`Successor Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the individual has the same rights as the consumer to seek and obtain redress from the supplier` (`Successor Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)

§§ `37. Preservation of other rights or remedies`

#ASSERT NOT `the Act restricts, limits or derogates from a right or remedy the consumer has apart from the Act` FALSE
#ASSERT `the Act restricts, limits or derogates from a right or remedy the consumer has apart from the Act` TRUE

§§ `38. Exemption from liability for publishers`

--                                                       prints on behalf of a supplier, good faith, ordinary course of business
#ASSERT `the person is not liable under the Act in respect of the advertisement` (`Publisher Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is not liable under the Act in respect of the advertisement` (`Publisher Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is not liable under the Act in respect of the advertisement` (`Publisher Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the person is not liable under the Act in respect of the advertisement` (`Publisher Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)

§§ `39. Parol evidence rule abolished`

--                                                                 express warranty evidence, consumer transaction, intended for business use
#ASSERT `section 39 makes the parol or extrinsic evidence admissible` (`Parol Evidence Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 39 makes the parol or extrinsic evidence admissible` (`Parol Evidence Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 39 makes the parol or extrinsic evidence admissible` (`Parol Evidence Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `section 39 makes the parol or extrinsic evidence admissible` (`Parol Evidence Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE)

§§ `40. Interpretation of documents`

#ASSERT `the provision must be interpreted against the supplier` (`Document Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the provision must be interpreted against the supplier` (`Document Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the provision must be interpreted against the supplier` (`Document Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the provision must be interpreted against the supplier` (`Document Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)

§§ `41. Burden of proof`

#ASSERT `the burden of proving compliance is on the supplier` (`Burden Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the burden of proving compliance is on the supplier` (`Burden Facts` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the burden of proving compliance is on the supplier` (`Burden Facts` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the burden of proving compliance is on the supplier` (`Burden Facts` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)

§§ `42 and 43. Amendment of Schedules; Regulations`

#ASSERT REFUSED `no orders under section 42 amending the Schedules after the date of the printed text are encoded in this model`
#ASSERT REFUSED `no regulations under section 43 are encoded in this model`

§§ `44. Saving and transitional provisions`

-- Transitional Facts: kind of matter, begun by or in relation to the Board, date begun, pending or unsatisfied on 2 April 2018,
-- the person acts in relation to the Commission instead.
`proceedings begun by the Board on 1 April 2018 and pending` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10`, TRUE, YMD 2018 4 1, TRUE, FALSE
`proceedings begun by the Board on 2 April 2018` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10`, TRUE, YMD 2018 4 2, TRUE, FALSE
`proceedings begun by the Board and no longer pending` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10`, TRUE, YMD 2018 3 1, FALSE, FALSE
`proceedings begun by someone else` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `proceedings for a declaration or an injunction under section 9 or 10`, FALSE, YMD 2018 3 1, TRUE, FALSE
`an investigation begun by the Board and pending` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `an investigation under Part 3A`, TRUE, YMD 2017 6 1, TRUE, FALSE
`an order made in relation to the Board, unsatisfied, now met by acting for the Commission` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board`, TRUE, YMD 2017 6 1, TRUE, TRUE
`an order made in relation to the Board, unsatisfied, not yet met` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board`, TRUE, YMD 2017 6 1, TRUE, FALSE
`an order made in relation to the Board, already satisfied` MEANS `Transitional Facts` OF `an order of the District Court or the High Court under section 9 or 10 requiring a person to notify, inform, reimburse or do anything in relation to the Board`, TRUE, YMD 2017 6 1, FALSE, TRUE

#ASSERT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `proceedings begun by the Board on 1 April 2018 and pending`
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `proceedings begun by the Board on 2 April 2018`
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `proceedings begun by the Board and no longer pending`
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `proceedings begun by someone else`
#ASSERT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `an investigation begun by the Board and pending`
#ASSERT NOT `the Commission may continue the matter as if it had commenced it` `an order made in relation to the Board, unsatisfied, not yet met`
#ASSERT `the unsatisfied order is satisfied` `an order made in relation to the Board, unsatisfied, now met by acting for the Commission`
#ASSERT NOT `the unsatisfied order is satisfied` `an order made in relation to the Board, unsatisfied, not yet met`
#ASSERT NOT `the unsatisfied order is satisfied` `an order made in relation to the Board, already satisfied`
#ASSERT NOT `the unsatisfied order is satisfied` `an investigation begun by the Board and pending`
